# andieswim-scraper — credentials and defaults
#
# Copy to `.env` (same directory as the scripts) and fill in what you need:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Nothing here ever reaches a command line, which is
# the point: a secret in argv is readable by anything that can run `ps` and
# lands in your shell history.
#
# Precedence, highest first:
#     an explicit flag  ->  an exported environment variable  ->  .env
#     ->  the flag's default
#
# So a value exported in your shell, by direnv or by CI is never clobbered
# by a file someone forgot to delete, and a flag you typed always wins.
#
# Check what was picked up, without printing secrets:
#
#     python3 env_config.py
#
# A placeholder left as it ships below — anything still carrying `{...}` —
# is treated as UNSET rather than sent to the API as if it were a key.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# READ THIS FIRST: on Andie Swim you probably need none of them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Measured 2026-09-18 from a datacenter address, with no key, no proxy and a
# plain browser User-Agent:
#
#     collection listings   HTTP 200
#     keyword search        HTTP 200
#     product documents     HTTP 200
#     the collection index  HTTP 200
#
# And with NO User-Agent header at all, with `curl/8.5.0`, with
# `python-urllib` and with a crawler UA: HTTP 200 every time. Twenty rapid
# requests in 4.9 s: twenty 200s. Nothing on the read path is gated.
#
# One captcha IS on this site and it is worth naming precisely rather than
# saying "none": Shopify's storefront-forms **hCaptcha** ships on every page
# the store serves (`ce_storefront_forms_captcha_hcaptcha.v1.5.3.iife.js`,
# sitekey f06e6c50-85a8-45c8-87d0-21a2b65856fe). It is bound to FORM SUBMITS
# — newsletter, contact, account creation — and no listing, product or JSON
# route renders one. A scrape never meets it. (If one ever appears on a read
# path, 2Captcha solves hCaptcha with `HCaptchaTaskProxyless`; this repo
# simply has no occasion to.)
#
# So the honest answer is that the paid products are OPTIONAL here, and what
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# WHAT DOES *NOT* BITE HERE (an inherited warning, re-measured and removed)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The repo this one was built from documents an edge that refuses a request
# whose User-Agent names an HTTP client library, by killing the connection
# rather than answering. That is a real behaviour of THAT site and it is
# FALSE here — CLAUDE.md §13: a number (or a warning) you inherited is not
# one you measured.
#
# Re-measured on this store, 2026-09-18, one URL, one address:
#   HTTP 200   no User-Agent header at all
#   HTTP 200   curl/8.5.0
#   HTTP 200   python-urllib/3.11
#   HTTP 200   a crawler UA
#   HTTP 200   an ordinary browser UA
#
# So you can script against this store with `requests` and nothing special.
# The only reason this repo drives a browser at all is the family's proxy,
# fingerprint and Scraping Browser paths, not access.


# --- 2Captcha ---------------------------------------------------------------
# One key, four separately-billed products: captcha solving, the Scraping
# Browser API, proxies and fingerprints. Get it at
# https://2captcha.com/enterpage
#
# Used here for --fingerprint, and for --solve-captcha if Andie Swim ever
# starts rendering a challenge. It renders none today.
TWOCAPTCHA_KEY=your_2captcha_api_key_here


# --- Scraping Browser API (CDP) ---------------------------------------------
# A managed Chrome you drive over CDP. The endpoint shape:
#
#   ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-{cc}-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222
#
# country-  picks the exit country. On this site that is what decides the
#           market a BARE host URL redirects to — pass a locale in the URL
#           and you control the market directly instead.
# pid-      a profile with persistent cookies. ONE live connection each, so
#           --concurrency is refused with --cdp-endpoint; use several pids,
#           one run each.
#
# NOTE these credentials expire in about a day. Never paste a working
# endpoint into a repo, a README or a workflow — get a fresh one from your
# dashboard when you need it.
ANDIESWIM_CDP_ENDPOINT=ws://{login}-zone-scraping_browser-country-de-pid-{profileId}:{password}@cb.2captcha.com:9222


# --- Proxy ------------------------------------------------------------------
# https://2captcha.com/proxy — residential and datacenter exits.
#
#   http://{user}:{password}@{cc}.proxy.2captcha.com:2334
#
# Region: match it to the market you are reading if you want the site's own
# geo-redirect to agree with your URL. A datacenter address was served
# normally on 2026-09-17, so this is about spreading volume and choosing a
# market rather than about getting in.
#
# Credentials are passed through the driver's own auth fields, never on the
# browser's command line. Selenium cannot authenticate a proxy at all — it
# strips the credentials and warns.
ANDIESWIM_PROXY=http://{user}:{password}@de.proxy.2captcha.com:2334


# --- Default target ---------------------------------------------------------
# Saves retyping --url. Andie Swim serves all 72 markets from ONE host,
# `www.andieswim.com`, with the market in the PATH — so there is no
# per-country hostname, and the locale segment is what selects the market.
#
# Category PATHS are localised and cannot be ported between markets:
# /en-fi/bags/backpacks is a real page and /de-de/bags/backpacks is an
# HTTP 404, because German addresses it as /de-de/lederwaren/… and Japanese
# percent-encodes its slugs.
#
#   a category listing   https://www.andieswim.com/en-us/writing-instruments
#   a keyword search     https://www.andieswim.com/en-us/search?q=fountain+pen
#   one product          https://www.andieswim.com/en-us/…-MB132460.html
#                        (needs --mode product, which reads its whole
#                        variant table — one row per nib width)
#
# Pagination is `?start=N&sz=24` on the listing URL itself, and the engines
# add it — you do not need to.
ANDIESWIM_URL=https://andieswim.com/collections/one-pieces
